1 NAME Remigio /de Segarra y López de Benavides/
2 GIVN Remigio
2 SURN de Segarra y López de Benavides
2 _MARNM de Segarra y López de Benavides
1 NAME D. Remigio de Segarra y de Benavides
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1745
2 ADDR
3 STAE Villa de San Germán
3 CTRY Puerto Rico
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 SEP 1794
2 ADDR
3 STAE Anasco
3 CTRY Puerto Rico
1 OCCU Fundador de Cabo Rojo
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://familysearch.org/pal:/MM9.2.1/398H-MMT
2 CONT
2 CONT Don Remigio Segarra is listed as one of the founders (founding settlers) of Cabo Rojo in 1771. His name along with his brothers, (D. Marcos, D. Manuel Antonio, D. Miguel) and father Capitan D. Juan Segarra are in the book entitled
2 CONC , Familias de Cabo Rojo by Acosta & Cuesta Camacho, as members of the group that are noted founders. 
2 CONT
2 CONT June 2015 Cabo Rojo San Miguel Arcangel Church 1791 Book lists Remigio as patrino for several children. Need to review this book entirely to determine more information about him. Book 1790-1791 page 26
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
